 "comments": [
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "Might be responsible for some of the extracellular antioxidant defense properties of selenium or might be involved in the transport of selenium. May supply selenium to tissues such as brain and testis"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "FUNCTION"
  },
  {
   "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
   "note": {
    "texts": [
     {
      "evidences": [
       {
        "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
        "source": "UniProtKB",
        "id": "P70274"
       }
      ],
      "value": "Passes from plasma into the glomerular filtrate where it is removed by endocytosis mediated by LRP2 in the proximal tubule epithelium"
     }
    ]
   },
   "subcellularLocations": [
    {
     "location": {
      "evidences": [
       {
        "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
        "source": "PubMed",
        "id": "8142465"
       }
      ],
      "value": "Secreted",
      "id": "SL-0243"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "Made in the liver and heart and secreted into the plasma. It is also found in the kidney"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250",
       "source": "UniProtKB",
       "id": "P70274"
      }
     ],
     "value": "The C-terminus is not required for endocytic uptake in the proximal tubule epithelium"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "DOMAIN"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "Phosphorylation sites are present in the extracellular medium"
    }
   ],
